WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.190
Every Monday, half my class arrives late.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.240
The head teacher asked me why.

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.610
I had a guess: maybe pupils are

4
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.850
tired after the weekend.

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.260
But a guess is not an answer.

6
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.690
So I asked the data.

7
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.290
Today: what data science is, and

8
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.650
how a teacher can use it.

9
00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.190
Data science means using data

10
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.250
to answer a question.

11
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.590
Data engineers collect and store the data.

12
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.880
Data scientists ask it questions, find

13
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.980
patterns, and explain what they mean.

14
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.700
Data science is a loop with four steps.

15
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.950
Ask a clear question.

16
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.170
Collect the data you need.

17
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.830
Explore it with numbers and charts.

18
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.370
Then explain what you found,

19
00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.030
and ask the next question.

20
00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.010
I took my register and counted late

21
00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:57.030
arrivals for four weeks, day by day.

22
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.020
Monday had twelve, the other

23
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.480
days only about three.

24
00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.500
The pattern was clear, and it was not

25
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.260
tiredness, because Friday was fine too.

26
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.780
So I asked the next question: how

27
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.420
do the late pupils travel?

28
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.290
Most came on the same bus.

29
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.580
On Mondays, it leaves the market late.

30
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.760
The data led us to the real cause.

31
00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.970
A good data question is clear, you

32
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:28.110
can measure it, and it is about

33
00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.490
something you can act on.

34
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.500
Are pupils happy is hard to measure.

35
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.980
How many pupils arrive late,

36
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.220
on which days, is easy.

37
00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:38.870
Quick check!

38
00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.330
Which is the better data question for a

39
00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:45.150
class: do pupils like reading, or how many

40
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.350
books did each pupil borrow this term?

41
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:49.790
Books borrowed this term.

42
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.830
You can count it from the library

43
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.690
cards, and compare classes.

44
00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:57.450
Liking reading matters too, but you would

45
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.530
need a careful survey to measure it.

46
00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.790
In the app, open Tidy tables.

47
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.160
A messy sheet gives the wrong answers.

48
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.410
Fix it step by step, and watch

49
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.770
the answers become right.

50
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:12.560
Your turn.

51
00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.570
We explained our finding.

52
00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.110
What comes next in the loop?

53
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.110
A new question.

54
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.590
Remember: data science

55
00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.370
answers questions with data.

56
00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.640
Ask, collect, explore,

57
00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.580
explain, and go round again.

58
00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.000
Try it in class tomorrow: ask your

59
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.020
pupils for one question about the

60
00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.780
school that data could answer.

61
00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.920
Write their ideas on the board.

62
00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.660
Choose one together that you can measure,

63
00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.160
and plan what to count this week.
